WEBVTT

00:05.790 --> 00:07.400
What the heck is that?!

00:07.950 --> 00:09.190
A nous.

00:09.720 --> 00:10.990
Nous Falaina.

00:11.730 --> 00:12.740
A nous?

00:13.550 --> 00:16.530
You mean the strange thing that was on your island?

00:17.710 --> 00:19.990
There's one on the Mud Whale too?

00:19.990 --> 00:24.890
The nous are like the hearts of the ships that float in the Sand Ocean.

00:24.890 --> 00:28.710
If its nous is destroyed, the Mud Whale will sink.

00:28.710 --> 00:30.040
Neri?

00:30.040 --> 00:32.230
So you've made it this far.

00:33.070 --> 00:37.340
Island girl, I see you have us figured out.

00:38.640 --> 00:40.900
However, it's too late!

00:41.600 --> 00:44.470
Do it! All is for the Mud Whale!

00:46.370 --> 00:46.690
Stop!

00:49.820 --> 00:51.030
No!

02:42.010 --> 02:43.890
What's happening this time?!

02:43.890 --> 02:46.020
The Mud Whale has never shaken this much before!

02:47.230 --> 02:48.480
What?!

02:56.360 --> 02:58.060
Seems like it's begun.

03:01.030 --> 03:01.880
Whoops!

03:02.410 --> 03:06.330
Don't give up now! Everyone will be dead in a few hours.

03:07.470 --> 03:11.100
Why don't we just keep playing until the end?

03:12.140 --> 03:13.790
Are we really going to sink?

03:13.790 --> 03:15.130
That's right.

03:15.130 --> 03:16.360
We'll all die.

03:16.360 --> 03:18.010
And you're okay with that?!

03:18.450 --> 03:19.470
I should ask you.

03:19.470 --> 03:22.930
Are you really that attached to your own life?

03:23.680 --> 03:25.390
Because I'm not.

03:27.140 --> 03:29.180
Living is a pain.

03:29.630 --> 03:31.830
Humans are bothersome creatures.

03:32.400 --> 03:36.230
Our hearts are the biggest nuisance.

03:36.600 --> 03:39.320
Let's liberate everyone with the power of the sand.

03:39.320 --> 03:43.450
Both you and I can be saved from the suffering of life!

03:46.090 --> 03:47.490
Don't decide for me.

03:47.920 --> 03:52.330
What you want to dispose of is your world alone.

03:52.650 --> 03:54.080
Not mine.

03:55.040 --> 03:58.240
My life is my own to decide!

04:00.530 --> 04:03.840
<i>We were born and raised on the Mud Whale.</i>

04:04.600 --> 04:06.180
<i>On this tiny world.</i>

04:07.210 --> 04:11.270
<i>What overwhelmed me the most about the outside world</i>

04:11.270 --> 04:17.510
<i>was learning that even there, the lives of so many different people intertwine.</i>

04:18.240 --> 04:20.910
<i>And yet each of their paths is not straightforward.</i>

04:21.430 --> 04:25.570
<i>They make up the colossal record of a vortex of blinding light and darkness.</i>

04:26.650 --> 04:28.280
<i>It scared me.</i>

04:28.530 --> 04:33.960
<i>That people, and the records of their lives, could vanish in an instant.</i>

04:35.370 --> 04:39.380
Keep going! Falaina's life must be completely extinguished!

04:40.710 --> 04:41.380
Lykos!

04:41.740 --> 04:43.280
Hurry up and fire!

04:43.280 --> 04:50.720
<i>No matter how painful or sad it may be, I do not want to ever give up my role as archivist.</i>

04:52.350 --> 04:58.380
<i>We do not yet wish to give up on ourselves.</i>

05:16.290 --> 05:17.500
Lykos!

05:21.830 --> 05:23.090
Stop...

05:23.090 --> 05:25.220
Please just stop already!

05:26.500 --> 05:29.570
You dumbass! The hell're you thinking hurting a comrade?!

05:30.490 --> 05:34.470
Everyone on the Mud Whale is like family!

05:35.650 --> 05:36.750
Why?

05:37.990 --> 05:41.770
Why is someone from the mainland trying to stop us?

05:42.610 --> 05:46.280
Are you not a soldier sent to destroy us?

05:47.280 --> 05:51.670
If Falaina is destroyed, the Mud Whale and all its people will sink.

05:52.670 --> 05:56.180
Is that not what your country wants?

05:57.380 --> 06:01.500
I... don't want that to happen.

06:01.850 --> 06:05.670
You are not sinners.

06:05.980 --> 06:11.920
You hold something important that we've lost.

06:11.920 --> 06:14.520
You are this world's hope.

06:14.520 --> 06:17.400
That is what I believe.

06:18.100 --> 06:18.850
Lykos!

06:20.900 --> 06:23.020
You call us hope?

06:23.720 --> 06:24.570
Preposterous.

06:25.610 --> 06:30.450
We have borne our sins for the last hundred years.

06:30.450 --> 06:36.300
To shed them, our only recourse is leaving this mortal plane.

06:36.870 --> 06:38.410
We are sinners!

06:38.410 --> 06:40.670
And who the hell decided that?!

06:41.020 --> 06:47.420
Are you saying that Lady Taisha and Sami and everyone else were sinners, so it was fine for them to die?

06:47.880 --> 06:50.380
Are you saying that's okay?!

06:51.120 --> 06:53.110
I don't know anything about the past.

06:53.110 --> 06:55.850
I don't know anything about
the people who attacked us either.

06:56.240 --> 07:02.230
You say it's hopeless, but Lykos came from the world outside and grew to love the Mud Whale!

07:02.720 --> 07:05.590
Is that not what you call hope?

07:05.590 --> 07:10.550
One day, other people out there may come to understand us too!

07:10.550 --> 07:12.990
What's wrong with believing in that?!

07:13.820 --> 07:18.040
As long as there's still hope, I don't want to run!

07:18.040 --> 07:22.310
I swear I'll protect Lykos and everyone else!

07:22.920 --> 07:25.270
Be silent!

07:27.230 --> 07:27.960
Move aside!

07:27.960 --> 07:28.800
No!

07:29.230 --> 07:29.920
Hurry!

07:30.260 --> 07:32.080
Shoot Falaina!

07:33.470 --> 07:35.100
What are you doing?!

07:39.940 --> 07:41.190
Let me see!

07:41.190 --> 07:43.610
We need to treat you.

07:43.610 --> 07:47.900
Rest easy. Most Unmarked are trained in medicine.

07:47.900 --> 07:49.820
Elder Shiraai! Elder Nashiji!

07:50.250 --> 07:53.450
Sorry, Hakuji. Take her to the infirmary.

07:53.910 --> 07:55.450
Hang in there.

08:03.970 --> 08:06.710
Why don't they understand?

08:07.280 --> 08:09.800
We did not decide this lightly.

08:10.520 --> 08:13.700
Why are they still hesitating?

08:15.560 --> 08:20.410
Hakuji. I was the one who summoned them here.

08:20.410 --> 08:21.180
Why?

08:21.180 --> 08:24.310
I've burdened you with unnecessary anxiety.

08:32.490 --> 08:34.700
I'm sorry, Mama.

09:00.950 --> 09:03.760
Did the shaking stop?

09:06.660 --> 09:08.800
<i>Did he do it?</i>

09:10.890 --> 09:15.280
Darn, the geezers chickened out at the last second.

09:15.280 --> 09:16.740
Hey, your eye...

09:17.280 --> 09:21.990
This is a false paradise. Everything is doomed to rot.

09:23.130 --> 09:26.820
The children of the whale are all born into this curse.

09:27.500 --> 09:34.090
It would be so much easier if we abandoned these decaying bodies and unneeded hearts.

09:36.690 --> 09:38.760
We'll finish our fight another day.

09:38.760 --> 09:41.310
I like saving my favorites for last.

09:42.020 --> 09:46.390
If I have to keep living, I want the fun to last.

09:48.720 --> 09:51.060
What was with all that rocking?

09:53.610 --> 09:54.600
It broke.

09:54.600 --> 09:56.610
Our jailbreaking tool!

09:56.960 --> 09:59.950
What now?! How are we supposed to save Suou?

09:59.950 --> 10:01.950
You're the one who fell on it.

10:01.950 --> 10:03.100
Lose some weight.

10:03.100 --> 10:04.910
Sh-Shut up.

10:17.470 --> 10:18.630
Elder Hakuji.

10:20.060 --> 10:28.020
I've lived my life with restraint, closing off my heart,
and doing what I thought right only to have it all fall apart...

10:29.050 --> 10:32.150
We have lost our way.

10:33.230 --> 10:38.030
What should we do for our island, our people?

10:49.640 --> 10:50.670
Here.

10:50.670 --> 10:54.150
Drink up. It'll help you relax.

10:54.660 --> 10:57.760
We promise not to lock you up anymore.

10:58.070 --> 11:00.010
You can rest easy.

11:08.350 --> 11:11.950
We must go and properly talk it through.

11:11.950 --> 11:13.460
To what end?

11:15.490 --> 11:19.820
If mass suicide is off the table, what should we...

11:20.210 --> 11:22.870
What should the children do?

11:24.530 --> 11:26.320
Have you seen Neri?

11:27.110 --> 11:27.910
Nope.

11:28.420 --> 11:32.610
<i>Where did she go? I have so much to ask her.</i>

11:55.400 --> 11:59.240
<i>Thank goodness the Mud Whale is still here.</i>

12:00.210 --> 12:01.910
Chakuro!

12:09.040 --> 12:11.040
Congratulations on becoming Chieftain.

12:11.040 --> 12:14.170
It suits you, Master Suou!

12:14.530 --> 12:17.170
We're your aides starting today.

12:17.510 --> 12:20.570
But I thought you served Lady Taisha.

12:20.570 --> 12:26.000
Normally the aides would be chosen again, but it's an emergency situation.

12:26.000 --> 12:30.770
We haven't asked the Council of Elders yet, but it's okay if we report it to them later.

12:32.350 --> 12:36.150
Then I'll be counting on you, unreliable as I am.

12:36.150 --> 12:39.910
We've got a problem if the Chieftain's
calling himself unreliable at a time like this.

12:39.910 --> 12:42.630
Just quit if you aren't up to it.

12:42.630 --> 12:44.950
Whew, talk about being blunt.

12:44.950 --> 12:46.280
Who're you calling blunt?

12:46.280 --> 12:49.410
Your attitude was totally different with Lady Taisha.

12:46.280 --> 12:47.380
It's only—

12:49.410 --> 12:50.540
Sh-Shut up.

12:51.760 --> 12:53.700
Come along now, Suou.

12:53.700 --> 12:55.090
Huh? To where?

12:55.090 --> 12:56.290
To see Lykos.

12:56.620 --> 12:59.530
She has something important to tell us.

13:00.130 --> 13:01.050
What about the Council?

13:01.050 --> 13:03.940
What?! You're way too naive.

13:03.940 --> 13:05.840
They can hear about it after.

13:05.840 --> 13:10.140
Honestly, I don't feel like we can trust them after what they've done.

13:10.140 --> 13:13.650
I know they did it for the Mud Whale's sake, but still.

13:16.200 --> 13:18.520
Should we be dividing ourselves at a time like this?

13:18.520 --> 13:20.730
We're just gathering information first.

13:20.730 --> 13:24.360
Fortunately, it seems like she's really opened up to Chakuro.

13:24.360 --> 13:28.490
Basically, Lykos is in the palm of our hand.

13:30.190 --> 13:34.920
I always thought the Chieftain's aides were just the Council's pawns.

13:34.920 --> 13:36.550
This time's special.

13:36.550 --> 13:38.250
We're doing it for our people.

13:38.940 --> 13:42.840
Both we and the Council are on the same page.

13:49.610 --> 13:50.550
Nous?

13:51.130 --> 13:56.160
The Elders were attempting to destroy that to sink the Mud Whale?

13:56.160 --> 13:56.890
Yes.

13:57.220 --> 14:00.170
Every ship has a nous on it!

14:00.170 --> 14:04.460
That means we can repel them by destroying their nous!

14:06.160 --> 14:11.690
But I guess if we do that, the people of your country will end up sinking.

14:11.690 --> 14:15.950
Don't worry. They have ways to safely return to the mother ship.

14:15.950 --> 14:18.450
They have a mother ship too?!

14:19.420 --> 14:24.170
Still, losing Skylos will be
a significant blow to their force.

14:24.170 --> 14:28.930
Is this "Skylos" the only battleship your country has?

14:28.930 --> 14:31.100
You stay out of this!

14:31.100 --> 14:32.430
Back off!

14:32.430 --> 14:33.810
I think it's fine.

14:34.350 --> 14:39.350
We need as much knowledge and experience as possible to put Chakuro's plan into action.

14:40.330 --> 14:43.190
You really think Masoo's got any useful knowledge?

14:43.190 --> 14:45.130
Shut up and go back to dying!

14:45.130 --> 14:46.930
Just sleep until you're healed!

14:46.930 --> 14:50.280
I'm fine and dandy, thanks! Why don't you just shut your mouth, musclehead?

14:50.280 --> 14:51.530
Please go on, Lykos.

14:52.090 --> 14:55.830
The Empire possesses eight nous ships in total.

14:56.230 --> 14:58.510
They have eight of those huge ships?!

14:58.510 --> 14:59.740
For real?

14:59.740 --> 15:01.250
They <i>only</i> have eight.

15:01.610 --> 15:04.590
The nous are creatures who eat emotions.

15:04.590 --> 15:08.340
Those who own the nous have the power to control the hearts of man.

15:08.340 --> 15:09.920
That's why my brother...

15:11.340 --> 15:14.600
Why they prioritized retrieving the nous Lykos.

15:15.020 --> 15:19.020
Why was your ship in shambles and all of the other people dead?

15:19.660 --> 15:21.480
Who did that?

15:21.980 --> 15:24.320
A ship from a country hostile to the Empire.

15:24.320 --> 15:26.120
There are even more out there?!

15:26.120 --> 15:27.230
Yes, several.

15:27.230 --> 15:31.610
You guys have eight of those huge ships with trained soldiers on each?

15:31.610 --> 15:35.990
And you all come from a bigger country,
plus there are other countries who fight you...

15:36.420 --> 15:38.680
And still other nations exist besides those?

15:38.680 --> 15:39.960
My head hurts.

15:40.760 --> 15:42.370
<i>Incredible!</i>

15:44.640 --> 15:47.090
<i>I'll have to tell Ouni about this later.</i>

15:47.090 --> 15:51.050
And they are our enemies as well?

15:54.560 --> 15:58.100
Only the Empire is trying to destroy the Mud Whale.

15:58.100 --> 16:01.350
The other countries don't even know of Falaina's existence.

16:01.850 --> 16:07.040
Why is the Empire trying to destroy the Mud Whale and Falaina?

16:07.040 --> 16:09.980
Falaina is different from the other nous.

16:09.980 --> 16:11.150
Different how?

16:11.510 --> 16:13.780
It can't eat people's emotions.

16:14.990 --> 16:20.270
And just as Falaina has a different nature from other nous, so did your ancestors from ours.

16:20.270 --> 16:20.790
Huh?

16:22.730 --> 16:30.380
Your ancestors rejected the control of the nous, and made the decision to live with emotions.

16:31.500 --> 16:37.140
Falaina, having failed its original purpose of eating emotions,

16:37.140 --> 16:42.270
was used by the Empire to imprison your ancestors in the Sand Ocean instead.

16:43.660 --> 16:49.910
We learned—I was taught that Falaina was full of barbarians who lived with emotions.

16:49.910 --> 16:57.740
That this small ship was a living hell
overflowing with hatred and distrust.

16:59.060 --> 17:03.050
Now that the Empire's adversaries have gained the ability to traverse the Sand Ocean,

17:03.050 --> 17:06.710
they can't risk Falaina falling into their hands.

17:07.850 --> 17:14.140
But even now, the Empire can't recognize or accept Falaina and its sinners.

17:15.040 --> 17:16.880
Their only choice...

17:18.070 --> 17:24.730
was to destroy Falaina and exterminate all of the sinners' descendants.

17:24.730 --> 17:29.480
B-But there might be people who aren't our enemies out there too, right?

17:29.890 --> 17:31.850
Somewhere in the outside world.

17:31.850 --> 17:35.240
Maybe, but I don't know anything about the other countries.

17:35.240 --> 17:40.090
Still, there's a huge difference between the entire world being our enemy and not.

17:40.090 --> 17:42.660
The enemy of my enemy is my friend, as they say.

17:43.600 --> 17:48.330
Do you think someone out there can find the Mud Whale and accept our existence?

17:50.180 --> 17:51.040
Lykos.

17:51.690 --> 17:54.670
Is it possible for us to wait for such a time?

17:55.910 --> 18:00.510
You'll need to withstand the Empire's attacks until then.

18:01.150 --> 18:04.060
Until we can find friends out there,

18:04.820 --> 18:08.690
do you think we can hold out and fight for hope?

18:10.410 --> 18:14.070
If that is what you wish, then I...

18:14.510 --> 18:18.070
I will put my life on the line to help.

18:22.530 --> 18:25.250
The new Chieftain has something to announce.

18:25.250 --> 18:28.330
I wonder what caused yesterday's shaking.

18:28.330 --> 18:29.570
It's the new Chieftain!

18:29.570 --> 18:31.290
It's Suou!

18:33.800 --> 18:38.930
<i>I get the feeling that there's more to the truth than what Lykos told us.</i>

18:39.990 --> 18:45.200
<i>Is there a deeper reason regarding our existence why the Empire wants to erase us?</i>

18:46.270 --> 18:49.980
<i>Either way, it's a fact that we have hope.</i>

18:52.600 --> 18:53.360
Everyone!

18:53.710 --> 18:55.100
He's starting.

18:56.760 --> 19:04.990
Do not forget that every day without fail, every year without fail, the sun and stars continue to bless us.

19:06.260 --> 19:10.110
They have never forsaken us.

19:10.710 --> 19:14.320
Neither the heavens nor the sands curse us.

19:12.970 --> 19:16.680
I'm amazed the Council approved this gathering.

19:16.680 --> 19:18.550
Suou, you can do it!

19:18.550 --> 19:26.680
I will now fully explain the situation we are in
and what actions I propose we take.

19:27.470 --> 19:31.200
We faced unprecedented tragedy only days ago.

19:31.200 --> 19:35.650
There are those of us who are still in mourning.

19:36.180 --> 19:40.200
Unfortunately, that will not be the last of it.

19:40.760 --> 19:46.330
We have knowledge that they are planning to attack once more four days from now.

19:49.770 --> 19:52.420
Please do not be overcome with despair!

19:52.420 --> 19:56.930
Now is the time for us to raise our heads.

19:56.930 --> 19:58.840
We must stand together!

19:59.900 --> 20:05.680
We must not stop until we have found others in the world who understand us and will take our side!

20:06.260 --> 20:09.710
I believe we must fight without being discouraged or intimidated.

20:11.420 --> 20:14.980
It's okay. There, there...

20:14.980 --> 20:16.360
To that end...

20:17.180 --> 20:21.820
I must rely on you Marked and your thymia.

20:23.900 --> 20:30.290
I've always wished to save you from the chains of your brief lifespans.

20:31.100 --> 20:32.280
And yet...

20:33.920 --> 20:35.640
I have accomplished nothing.

20:37.460 --> 20:41.510
And now I must request this of you.

20:50.480 --> 20:52.640
You're the only one here who's still weak-willed!

20:53.710 --> 20:58.170
We all accepted the curse of our short lives long ago.

20:58.170 --> 21:00.480
And we'll do the same however our fates may change!

21:01.050 --> 21:05.160
All you need to do is stand proud and order us to fight!

21:05.830 --> 21:06.740
Ouni?

21:08.300 --> 21:11.620
Will you... lend your strength as well?

21:22.140 --> 21:22.920
I will.

21:28.340 --> 21:29.720
Good grief.

21:46.960 --> 21:50.870
<i>Nobody could tell whether our choice was right or wrong.</i>

21:52.160 --> 21:54.450
<i>Four days remained until Skylos' full assault.</i>

21:55.830 --> 21:58.960
<i>That was the only thing we knew for certain.</i>
